      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIN KIATA (2) looks to have a fair bit of upside after leading all the way here just over 2 weeks ago, and he gets to chase a hat-trick of wins here by remaining in the same class. The extra 2.5kg should not be enough to stop him from getting the job done again. FLAMING NAVY (1) was put aside after failing to handle a couple of wet tracks in the winter, and he has been kept ticking over at the trials last month. He slides down in class and is ready to rumble. Each way value. STARGUST (4) motored home too late when finishing runner-up by a nose here just over 2 weeks ago, and the rise in class will hold no fear for this gelding. He carries 4.5kg less and can go one better. FOREVER WAITING (5) was a soft winner fresh up in a modest field at Naracoorte, and he hit the line strongly in his last couple of starts, including a narrowly beaten fourth here by less than a length last start. Follow your money. SCENIC HOST (3) is a durable veteran who usually improves quickly with racing.",
